#: ../../source/developer-guides/customize-model.md:468
#: d9562e29d4f34bacb447b6db181df755
msgid "常见问题与避坑指南"
msgstr "Common Pitfalls and Best Practices"

#: ../../source/developer-guides/customize-model.md:471
#: 2f98ff57f8e74c859c73f0eebb6377f6
msgid ""
"**张量未放置到对应设备**：在 `build_components` 中构建图矩阵、先验知识矩阵时，不要使用 "
"`self.device_`（此时模型尚未 `build()`）。应统一读取 `rc.general.device`，或使用 "
"`self.model.register_buffer(...)` 交由 PyTorch 托管设备迁移。"
msgstr ""
"**Tensors Not on Correct Device**: When constructing graph matrices or "
"prior knowledge tables in `build_components`, do not use `self.device_` "
"(since `build()` has not run yet). Read `rc.general.device` instead, or "
"call `self.model.register_buffer(...)` so PyTorch handles device "
"transfers automatically."

#: ../../source/developer-guides/customize-model.md:472
#: 9fbd694c73f446208a6635b6e2de2206
msgid ""
"**预测与标签对齐错位**：绝不要在模型内部手写 `y[:, :-1]` 与 `mask[:, 1:]` 的展平截断逻辑！必须统一调用 "
"`self._extract_valid_predictions(y_hat_full, response, mask, "
"same_position=...)`。如果是 DKT 这种在相同位置预测当前题目的模型，传入 "
"`same_position=True`；如果是预测下一题的模型，传入 `same_position=False`。"
msgstr ""
"**Misaligned Predictions and Labels**: Never manually write flattening "
"and slicing logic like `y[:, :-1]` and `mask[:, 1:]` inside models! "
"Always call `self._extract_valid_predictions(y_hat_full, response, mask, "
"same_position=...)`. Pass `same_position=True` for same-position models "
"like DKT, and `same_position=False` for next-item models."

#: ../../source/developer-guides/customize-model.md:473
#: af27745130fc4793a7fbbfb17ff4654a
msgid ""
"**空批次崩溃**：在极端过滤或填充序列的末尾，偶尔会出现该 batch 内完全没有有效掩码点的情况。务必在 "
"`_extract_valid_predictions` 后调用 `self._handle_empty_batch(y_hat, "
"y_label)`，避免 BCELoss 遇到零维张量触发 CUDA 异常。"
msgstr ""
"**Empty Batch Crashes**: Under extreme filtering or at sequence tails, a "
"batch might occasionally contain zero valid masked positions. Always "
"invoke `self._handle_empty_batch(y_hat, y_label)` after "
"`_extract_valid_predictions` to prevent BCELoss from triggering CUDA "
"runtime errors on zero-sized tensors."
